Now I have everything I need. Here is the full academic smell audit:

---

## testsmells.org 19-Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 / .NET 10 · **Scope:** 8 test methods in 1 class
**Integration calibration:** Class is tagged `[TestCategory("Integration")]` — Mystery Guest, Eager Test, and Sleepy Test severity are calibrated accordingly.

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Total    | 4           | 4              |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### ❶ Conditional Test Logic — **High**

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101-108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** The `if`/`else` means only one branch ever executes per run. The other branch's assertion is silently skipped — a hidden testing gap. If `loaded` is never a `PremiumUser`, the discount-rate path is dead code.

**Fix — split into two tests with explicit data:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscountRate()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "VIP", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com");
    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<PremiumUser>(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(((PremiumUser)loaded).DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One branch is guaranteed untested — bugs in that path will never be caught.

---

#### ❷ Sleepy Test — **High** *(not downgraded — sleep is a smell even for integration tests)*

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Problem:** Hard-codes a 3-second wall-clock wait. Makes the suite slow, and if the notification mechanism takes slightly longer under load the test becomes flaky. Also uses `Thread.Sleep` inside an `async Task` method, blocking the thread pool thread.

**Fix — poll with a timeout:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await PollUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}

private static async Task<bool> PollUntilAsync(Func<bool> condition, TimeSpan timeout)
{
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow + timeout;
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (condition()) return true;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
    return false;
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Adds 3 s to every run; will produce false failures under CI load.

---

#### ❸ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — **High**

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113-119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Problem:** Zero assertions. The test passes as long as no exception is thrown — if `Insert` silently discards every row, this test still goes green.

**Fix — assert the observable outcome:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — the test inflates pass counts and coverage while verifying nothing.

---

#### ❹ Assertion Roulette — **Medium**

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35-38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Problem:** Four assertions, none with a message parameter. When one fails, the MSTest output shows only `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<(null)>` — no hint about *which property* was wrong or *why* it matters.

**Fix — add descriptive messages:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-assigned on insert.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower diagnosis on CI failures — developers must open the code to locate which assertion failed.

---

### Smells Not Detected (11 of 19 clean)

| Smell | Status |
|-------|--------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean — SQLite in-memory is hermetic; integration-calibrated |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean — max 3 production methods per test; integration-calibrated |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean — `3`, `10`, `100` are all contextually obvious counts |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean — no `ToString()` comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean — no `try`/`catch` in tests |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean — `_connection` and `_repository` used by all 8 tests |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean — no `[Ignore]` attributes |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean — shared method calls are setup, not primary actions |
| Redundant Print / Redundant Assertion / Default Test / Constructor Init / Empty Test / Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean |

### Smell-Free Highlights

`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`, `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord`, `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`, and `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` are well-structured: clear arrange-act-assert, meaningful assertions, no control flow, and appropriate scope for integration tests.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` after bulk insert | ~2 min |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into two focused tests | ~10 min |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll-until helper | ~15 min |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | Add message strings to 4 assertions | ~5 min |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests are clean and well-designed. The remaining 4 each carry exactly one academic smell. Fixes 1 and 4 are quick wins; fix 2 eliminates a hidden testing gap; fix 3 removes flakiness risk and shaves 3 seconds off every run.
